      "generated_file": null
    },
    {
      "diff": "@@ -18,14 +18,14 @@ __We do not ship official 32-bit Windows packages for Wireshark 4.0 and later__.\n If you need to use Wireshark on that platform, we recommend using the latest 3.6 release.\n wsbuglink:17779[]\n \n-* The Windows installers now ship with Qt 5.12.2.\n-They previously shipped with Qt 6.2.3.\n+// * The Windows installers now ship with Qt 5.12.2.\n+// They previously shipped with Qt 6.2.3.\n \n === Bug Fixes\n \n // The following vulnerabilities have been fixed:\n \n-// * wssalink:2022-07[]\n+// * wssalink:2022-09[]\n // Foo dissector {crash,infinite loop,memory leak}.\n // wsbuglink:xxxxx[].\n // cveidlink:2022-xxxx[].\n@@ -42,32 +42,12 @@ The following bugs have been fixed:\n //* cveidlink:2014-2486[]\n //* Wireshark insists on subscribing to two dozen streaming services but only watches three.\n \n-* Comparing a boolean field against 1 always succeeds on big-endian machines. wsbuglink:12236[].\n-* Qt: MaxMind GeoIP columns not added to Endpoints table. wsbuglink:18320[].\n-* Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2022-10-04-7131.pcap. wsbuglink:18402[].\n-* The RTP player might not play audio on Windows. wsbuglink:18413[].\n-* Wireshark 4.0 breaks display filter expression with > sign. wsbuglink:18418[].\n-* Capture filters not working when using SSH capture and dumpcap. wsbuglink:18420[].\n-* Packet diagram field values are not terminated. wsbuglink:18428[].\n-* Packet bytes not displayed completely if scrolling. wsbuglink:18438[].\n-* Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2022-10-13-7166.pcap. wsbuglink:18467[].\n-* Decoding bug H.245 userInput Signal. wsbuglink:18468[].\n-* CFDP dissector doesn't handle \\\"destination filename\\\" only. wsbuglink:18495[].\n-* Home page capture button doesn't pop up capture options dialog. wsbuglink:18506[].\n-* Missing dot in H.248 protocol name. wsbuglink:18513[].\n-* Missing dot for protocol H.264 in protocol column. wsbuglink:18524[].\n-* Fuzz job crash output: fuzz-2022-10-23-7240.pcap. wsbuglink:18534[].\n \n === New and Updated Features\n \n \n === Removed Features and Support\n \n-* The experimental display filter syntax for literals using angle brackets <...>\n-  that was introduced in Wireshark 4.0.0 has been removed. For byte arrays a colon prefix\n-  can be used instead.\n-  See the https://www.wireshark.org/docs/wsug_html_chunked/ChWorkBuildDisplayFilterSection.html#_some_protocol_names_can_be_ambiguous[User’s Guide] for details.\n-\n // === Removed Dissectors\n \n // === New File Format Decoding Support\n@@ -86,36 +66,15 @@ There are no new protocols in this release.\n // ag -A1 '(define PSNAME|proto_register_protocol[^_])' $(git diff --name-only v4.0.1.. | ag packet- | sort -u)\n [commaize]\n --\n-ASN.1 PER\n-CFDP\n-Diameter\n-DirectPlay\n-F5 Ethernet Trailer\n-GTP\n-H.223\n-H.248\n-H.264\n-H.265\n-IEEE 802.11\n-IPv4\n-MBIM\n-O-RAN FH CUS\n-PFCP\n-RTCP\n-SCTP\n-SMB\n-TCP\n-TRANSUM\n --\n \n === New and Updated Capture File Support\n \n-// There is no new or updated capture file support in this release.\n+There is no new or updated capture file support in this release.\n // Add one file type per line between the -- delimiters.\n-[commaize]\n---\n-BLF\n---\n+// [commaize]\n+// --\n+// --\n \n // === New and Updated Capture Interfaces support\n \n",
      "collapsed": false,
      "too_large": false,
      "new_path": "docbook/release-notes.adoc",
      "old_path": "docbook/release-notes.adoc",
